<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title>PDF Book Store Project Description</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: "Nirmala UI", "Segoe UI", Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.55; color: #222; }
    h1 { color: #0f5b55; font-size: 26px; }
    h2 { color: #b45309; font-size: 20px; margin-top: 24px; }
    h3 { color: #0f5b55; font-size: 16px; margin-top: 18px; }
    p, li { font-size: 12.5pt; }
    code { background: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 5px; border-radius: 4px; }
    table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 12px 0; }
    th, td { border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 8px; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
    th { background: #fff3e4; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Mahesh Bharti PDF Book Store - Project Description</h1>
  <p>
    Ye project ek full-stack PDF e-book selling website hai. Isme user books browse karta hai, login/signup OTP se account verify karta hai,
    payment karta hai, aur successful payment ke baad apni purchased PDF library me book read kar sakta hai. Admin panel se books,
    orders, payment settings, quote section, users aur support tickets manage kiye ja sakte hain.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Technology Stack</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Part</th><th>Technology</th><th>Kaam</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Frontend</td><td>React, Vite, Tailwind CSS</td><td>User interface, routes, cart, checkout, dashboard, admin panel</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Backend</td><td>Node.js, Express.js</td><td>REST API, authentication, payment verification, admin APIs</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Database</td><td>MongoDB with Mongoose</td><td>Users, books, orders, OTP, settings, support tickets store karna</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Auth</td><td>JWT + OTP</td><td>Secure login/signup, one active session, protected pages</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Payment</td><td>Razorpay + Manual UPI</td><td>Online payment verification aur UPI screenshot admin verification</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Deployment</td><td>Vercel frontend, Render backend</td><td>Live hosting</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>2. Folder Structure</h2>
  <p><code>client</code> folder me frontend code hai. <code>server</code> folder me backend API code hai.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>client/src/pages</code>: user pages jaise Home, Books, Checkout, Login, Library, Admin pages.</li>
    <li><code>client/src/components</code>: shared UI components jaise Layout, BookCard, AdminShell.</li>
    <li><code>client/src/context</code>: AuthContext aur CartContext, jisse login state aur cart app me share hota hai.</li>
    <li><code>server/src/controllers</code>: business logic, jaise auth, books, payment, admin, quote, support.</li>
    <li><code>server/src/models</code>: MongoDB schemas, jaise User, Book, Order, Otp.</li>
    <li><code>server/src/routes</code>: API endpoints ko controllers se connect karta hai.</li>
    <li><code>server/src/middleware</code>: authentication, validation, upload, rate limit, error handling.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Frontend Kaise Kaam Karta Hai</h2>
  <p>
    Frontend React single-page app hai. User page change karta hai to browser reload nahi hota; React Router route ke hisaab se component dikhata hai.
    Ab pages lazy-load hote hain, matlab first load par sirf zaroori code download hota hai. Isse slow internet par website jaldi open hoti hai.
  </p>
  <h3>Main User Flow</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>User Home page par quote section, hero books aur featured books dekhta hai.</li>
    <li>Books page par search karke books dekh sakta hai.</li>
    <li>Book details page par price, description aur buy button hota hai.</li>
    <li>Cart me add karke checkout par ja sakta hai.</li>
    <li>Payment successful hone ke baad Library me book unlock hoti hai.</li>
    <li>PDF Reader secure in-app reading ke liye PDF ko authenticated API se blob ke form me open karta hai.</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>Frontend Performance Improvements</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>React routes lazy-loaded kiye gaye, isse initial JavaScript bundle chhota hua.</li>
    <li>Images me <code>loading="lazy"</code> aur <code>decoding="async"</code> add kiya gaya.</li>
    <li>Book detail cover image ko high priority diya gaya taki main image fast dikhe.</li>
    <li>Quote animation CSS level par chalti hai, jisse page khula rahe tab bhi visible rahe.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Backend Kaise Kaam Karta Hai</h2>
  <p>
    Backend Express server hai. Ye APIs provide karta hai, database se data read/write karta hai, JWT authentication verify karta hai,
    OTP generate/verify karta hai, payment verify karta hai, aur admin panel ke actions handle karta hai.
  </p>

  <h3>Important Backend APIs</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><code>/api/auth/signup</code>: user signup aur OTP send.</li>
    <li><code>/api/auth/verify-otp</code>: signup OTP verify karke account active.</li>
    <li><code>/api/auth/login/request-otp</code>: login OTP send.</li>
    <li><code>/api/auth/login/verify-otp</code>: OTP verify karke JWT token issue.</li>
    <li><code>/api/books</code>: public book listing.</li>
    <li><code>/api/books/:id/download</code>: protected PDF download/read endpoint.</li>
    <li><code>/api/payments/create-order</code>: Razorpay ya manual UPI order create.</li>
    <li><code>/api/payments/verify</code>: Razorpay signature verify karke order success.</li>
    <li><code>/api/payments/confirm-manual</code>: UPI payment screenshot submit.</li>
    <li><code>/api/admin/orders/:id/status</code>: admin order approve/fail karta hai.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Backend Performance Improvements</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Public book listing aur book details queries me <code>lean()</code> use kiya gaya, jisse MongoDB read faster hota hai.</li>
    <li>Books API par short browser/proxy cache header lagaya gaya.</li>
    <li>Quote API par cache header lagaya gaya taki repeat requests fast ho.</li>
    <li>Static covers, quote images aur QR images cacheable hain.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Authentication and OTP</h2>
  <p>
    User signup/login OTP based hai. OTP email/SMS ke through send hota hai. OTP bcrypt hash ke form me database me store hota hai,
    plain OTP database me save nahi hota. OTP expire time 10 minutes hai. Wrong OTP par ab card ke andar input ke niche
    <b>Invalid OTP</b> message dikhata hai, generic server error nahi.
  </p>
  <p>
    Login ke baad backend JWT token deta hai. Token me user id, role aur active session id hota hai. Agar user dusre device par login karta hai,
    old session invalid ho jata hai. Isse account sharing aur unauthorized access ka risk kam hota hai.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Payment System</h2>
  <h3>Razorpay Online Payment</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>User checkout par Razorpay choose karta hai.</li>
    <li>Backend Razorpay order create karta hai.</li>
    <li>Frontend Razorpay checkout open karta hai.</li>
    <li>Payment ke baad Razorpay response backend ko bheja jata hai.</li>
    <li>Backend secret key se HMAC signature generate karke received signature se compare karta hai.</li>
    <li>Signature match hone par order success hota hai aur PDF library unlock hoti hai.</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>Manual UPI Payment</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>User UPI option choose karta hai.</li>
    <li>Backend order amount ke saath UPI QR/payment URI generate karta hai.</li>
    <li>User payment karke screenshot upload karta hai.</li>
    <li>Order status submitted hota hai.</li>
    <li>Admin panel se proof check karke success ya failed status set karta hai.</li>
    <li>Success hone par PDF unlock hoti hai.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>7. Security Measures</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>JWT secret minimum 32 characters required hai.</li>
    <li>Protected APIs me Bearer token verify hota hai.</li>
    <li>Admin APIs role check ke bina accessible nahi hain.</li>
    <li>Razorpay signature timing-safe compare se verify hota hai.</li>
    <li>Razorpay webhook signature bhi timing-safe compare se verify hota hai.</li>
    <li>Payment proof images public folder se remove karke admin-only protected API se open hoti hain.</li>
    <li>Manual payment proof already submitted/success order par dobara submit nahi ho sakta.</li>
    <li>PDF download sirf paid success order aur 30-day access window me allowed hai.</li>
    <li>PDF file path upload directory ke andar lock kiya gaya hai.</li>
    <li>File upload me image/PDF type aur size limit check hota hai.</li>
    <li>Rate limiting login, OTP, payment aur admin writes par active hai.</li>
    <li>Helmet security headers aur CORS origin restrictions enabled hain.</li>
    <li>Email HTML content escape kiya gaya hai, jisse injection risk kam hota hai.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. Admin Panel</h2>
  <p>
    Admin panel me dashboard stats, books management, orders, payment settings, quote settings, users aur support tickets manage hote hain.
    Admin signup Gmail OTP se verify hota hai. Agar ek verified admin exist karta hai to new admin signup block hota hai.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Quote Section</h2>
  <p>
    Home page ke top par quote card hai. Admin panel se quote, author name aur author image update ho sakta hai.
    Quote content 4 hours ke slot ke hisaab se rotate hota hai. Quote text par navbar jaisa falling-letter animation sirf quote ke letters par lagaya gaya hai.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Deployment Setup</h2>
  <h3>Backend on Render</h3>
  <p>
    <code>render.yaml</code> file backend deployment define karti hai. Root directory <code>server</code>, build command <code>npm install</code>,
    start command <code>npm start</code> hai. Important environment variables: <code>MONGO_URI</code>, <code>JWT_SECRET</code>,
    <code>CLIENT_URL</code>, SMTP settings, Razorpay keys, UPI settings.
  </p>

  <h3>Frontend on Vercel</h3>
  <p>
    Frontend <code>client</code> folder se deploy hota hai. Build command <code>npm run build</code> hai aur output directory <code>dist</code>.
    Environment variable <code>VITE_API_URL</code> backend API URL par set hoti hai.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Local Setup Steps</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Project folder open karein.</li>
    <li>Server dependencies install: <code>npm install --prefix server</code></li>
    <li>Client dependencies install: <code>npm install --prefix client</code></li>
    <li>Server me <code>.env</code> file banakar MongoDB, JWT, SMTP, Razorpay, UPI values set karein.</li>
    <li>Backend run: <code>npm run dev --prefix server</code></li>
    <li>Frontend run: <code>npm run dev --prefix client</code></li>
    <li>Browser me Vite URL open karein, normally <code>http://localhost:5173</code>.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>12. Recent Work Summary</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Wrong OTP server error ko invalid OTP inline message me convert kiya.</li>
    <li>Quote animation sirf quote text par visible infinite falling effect banaya.</li>
    <li>Quote content 4 hours me change hone wala logic add kiya.</li>
    <li>Payment flow aur PDF access security harden kiya.</li>
    <li>Manual payment proofs ko private/protected banaya.</li>
    <li>Frontend lazy loading aur image optimization add kiya.</li>
    <li>Backend public reads fast karne ke liye lean queries aur cache headers add kiye.</li>
    <li>Client/server production dependency audit me 0 vulnerabilities confirm hua.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>13. Testing and Verification</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Frontend production build: <code>npm run build</code> successful.</li>
    <li>Server changed files syntax check successful.</li>
    <li>Client production dependencies audit: 0 vulnerabilities.</li>
    <li>Server production dependencies audit: 0 vulnerabilities.</li>
    <li>Payment and PDF access flow manually reviewed for security risks.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>14. Simple Explanation for Presentation</h2>
  <p>
    Is project me humne ek digital PDF book store banaya hai jahan user secure OTP login ke through account banata hai,
    books browse karta hai, Razorpay ya UPI ke through payment karta hai, aur successful payment ke baad secure library me PDF read kar sakta hai.
    Backend payment verification, user authentication, PDF access control aur admin management handle karta hai. Frontend user-friendly mobile aur laptop UI provide karta hai.
    Security ke liye token-based login, OTP hashing, rate limiting, protected admin APIs, private payment proofs aur verified payment ke bina PDF access block kiya gaya hai.
  </p>
</body>
</html>
